  "output": "Based on the files shown (this is a repeated audit — memory shows this exact analysis has run several times already; findings below are consistent with those but grounded in the actual code snippets provided here).\n\n## 1. N+1 / redundant fetch patterns\n\n**`src/api.ts` — no response cache on read-heavy, rarely-changing endpoints**\n`phrases()`, `outcomes()`, `languageSettings()` etc. all go through the same `request()` with no caching, so every view mount re-fetches static reference data. You already have a cache utility (`src/utils/cache.ts`) sitting unused for this purpose.\n\n```ts\n// src/api.ts\nasync function cachedRequest<T>(key: string, path: string, ttlMs = 60_000): Promise<T> {\n  const hit = cacheGet<{ v: T; t: number } | null>(key, null);\n  if (hit && Date.now() - hit.t < ttlMs) return hit.v;\n  const value = await request<T>(path);\n  cacheSet(key, { v: value, t: Date.now() });\n  return value;\n}\n// use for: phrases, outcomes, languageSettings\n```\n\n## 2. Unnecessary re-renders\n\n**`src/utils/transcript.ts` — `buildConversationItems()` is O(n) filter+map+sort, called from render**\nIf a view calls this directly in the render body (not in `useMemo`), it recomputes on every parent re-render even when `transcript`/`events` haven't changed.\n\n```ts\nconst items = useMemo(\n  () => buildConversationItems(transcript, events),\n  [transcript, events]\n);\n```\n\n**Campaign strategy objects** (per earlier audit, `CampaignsView`) — rebuilding a strategy object literal each render breaks referential equality for memoized children/effects keyed on it. Wrap construction in `useMemo` keyed on the campaign id/version.\n\n## 3. Caching opportunities\n\n- `src/utils/cache.ts` (`cacheGet`/`cacheSet`) is a solid localStorage cache but has zero call sites shown in this batch of files — it's infrastructure without consumers. Wire it into `api.ts` as above.\n- No `Cache-Control`/ETag handling on the fetch side in `request()` — even trivial `if (response.headers.get('etag'))` short-circuiting would help for polling views (transcripts, call events).\n\n## 4. Memory leaks\n\n**`src/hooks/useCountUp.ts`** — `requestAnimationFrame` loop has no cancellation on unmount/target-change mid-flight:\n\n```ts\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (target === 0) { setValue(0); return; }\n  const start = performance.now();\n  ref.current?.classList.add('counting');\n  let raf: number;\n  const tick = (now: number) => {\n    const progress = Math.min((now - start) / duration, 1);\n    const eased = 1 - Math.pow(1 - progress, 3);\n    setValue(Math.round(target * eased));\n    if (progress < 1) raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n    else ref.current?.classList.remove('counting');\n  };\n  raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n  return () => cancelAnimationFrame(raf); // missing today\n}, [target, duration]);\n```\nWithout this, rapid target changes (e.g. dashboard stat updating while animating) stack overlapping RAF loops that keep calling `setValue` on a value that's already stale, and can call `setValue` after the component unmounts.\n\n**`useToasts.ts`** — `setTimeout(() => dismissToast(id), durationMs)` is never cleared if the component unmounts before it fires or if `dismissToast` is called manually first; harmless in practice (state setter is a no-op post-unmount in React 18) but still worth tracking the timer id and clearing it in `dismissToast`/cleanup to avoid the dangling timer reference.\n\n## 5. Redundant computations\n\n- `src/utils/cache.ts` — `pruneOldCache()` runs a full `localStorage` linear scan **on module import**, i.e. once per page load, which is fine at current scale but would benefit from a sessionStorage \"already pruned this session\" flag if `localStorage` grows large from other apps sharing the origin.\n- `src/utils/formatting.ts` — `parseApiDate` re-runs the timezone regex test and `new Date()` construction independently in `formatDate`, `formatTime`, and `timeAgo`, each called separately per row in list views (transcripts, audit log). For large lists, precompute the parsed date once per row and pass it to whichever formatter is needed instead of re-parsing per column.\n\n## Priority\n1. Cancel the RAF in `useCountUp` (real leak, low risk to fix).\n2. Wrap `buildConversationItems` call site in `useMemo`.\n3. Add a short-TTL cache layer to `api.ts` for phrases/outcomes/languageSettings.\n\nWant me to apply the `useCountUp` cancellation fix and the `useMemo` wrap now, since those are concrete and low-risk?\n",
